I come out of the clinic.
The doctor's prescription is in my hand.
I need to get the medicine now.
There is a medical store on the way home.
I stop there to get my medicines.
A young man is standing at the counter.
I say to him, "Dada, give me these medicines."
I give the doctor's prescription to him.
He reads the prescription carefully.
He says, "Madam, wait for two minutes."
He gives me two strips of tablets and one bottle of cough syrup.
I ask him, "How many rupees is this?"
He says, "Three hundred and fifty rupees."
I give him the money.
He puts the medicines in a bag and gives it to me.
He says, "You should take the medicine on time and rest completely."
I thank him.
Now I just want to go home quickly.
My throat is still hurting a lot.
